      "description": "Founded in 1817, the University of Michigan was originally located in Detroit, before relocating to Ann Arbor in 1837, at the time of the statehood of Michigan.  The campus developed initially around the Diag, a quad, with the first buildings being constructed in the 1840s and 1850s in the Greek Revival style, of which only a single building remains.  The university grew significantly in the late 19th Century and early 20th Century, with the prestige of the university growing alongside the wealth and population of the state of Michigan.  The university today is the oldest and most prestigious institution of higher learning in Michigan, with approximately 50,000 students.",
